Title: simple way te to compute rgb buffer from I420 frame ffmpeg.
Body: <p>I'm trying to compute directly rgb buffer from avframe. Something is going wrong since the obtained image is wrong. Extracting grey image from AVFrame-&gt;data[0] is working fine. However I'm not able to extract colored image</p>
<pre><code>inline void YCrCb_to_RGB8(int Y, int Cr, int Cb, int&amp; R, int&amp; G, int&amp; B){

   R = (int)(Y + 1.402 *(Cr - 128));
   G = (int)(Y - 0.344136*(Cb-128) -0.71414*(Cr-128));
   B = (int)(Y + 1.772 *(Cb-128));

   if (R &lt; 0) R = 0; else if (R &gt; 255) R = 255;
   if (G &lt; 0) G = 0; else if (G &gt; 255) G = 255;
   if (B &lt; 0) B = 0; else if (B &gt; 255) B = 255;
}

int getRGB8buffer(AVFrame* pFrame, byte* buffer){

   const int width = pFrame-&gt;width, height = pFrame-&gt;height;
   int Y, Cr, Cb;
   int R, G, B;

   int pixel = 0;
   for (int y = 0; y &lt; height; y++)
   {
    for (int x = 0; x &lt; width; x++)
    {

        Y = pFrame-&gt;data[0][x + y * width];
        Cr = pFrame-&gt;data[1][x / 2 + ((int)(y / 2)) * pFrame-&gt;linesize[1]];
        Cb = pFrame-&gt;data[2][x / 2 + ((int)(y / 2)) * pFrame-&gt;linesize[2]];

        YCrCb_to_RGB8(Y, Cr, Cb, R, G, B);
        buffer[pixel * 3 + 0] = R;
        buffer[pixel * 3 + 1] = G;
        buffer[pixel * 3 + 2] = B;
        pixel++;
    }
   }
   return 0;
}
</code></pre>
<p>When I save the obtained image as ppm using</p>
<pre><code>int save_RGB_frame(unsigned char* buf, int wrap, int xsize,int ysize, const char* filename){

   FILE* f;
   int i;
   f = fopen(filename, &quot;w&quot;);
   // portable ppm format -&gt; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netpbm#PPM_example
   fprintf(f, &quot;P6\n%d %d\n%d\n&quot;, xsize, ysize, 255);

   // writing line by line
   for (i = 0; i &lt; ysize; i++)
      fwrite(buf + i * wrap, 1, xsize*3, f);
   fclose(f);

   return 0;
 }
</code></pre>
<p>The resulting image is wrong
link the the resulting image <a href="https://github.com/hacenesh/ffmpeg_question/blob/main/img_2028144.ppm" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://github.com/hacenesh/ffmpeg_question/blob/main/img_2028144.ppm</a></p>

Title: React Native: Cannot position Image with resizeMode &quot;contain&quot; at the flex-end of parent component.
Body: <p>So I'm trying to animate two images by sliding them out of the screen in opposite directions in React Native. The 2 images are positioned side by side, <strong>with each image's parent component taking up 50% of the screen width</strong>. I want the images to be positioned next to each other without any gap between them, AND they also have to use <code>resizeMode=&quot;contain&quot;</code> to ensure that the images <strong>scale proportionally</strong> to fit within their respective containers, <strong>while preserving their aspect ratios</strong>.</p>
<p>I have tried everything that I can think of to position the left-hand Image component to the very end of its parent component, and the right-hand Image to the very start of its parent component so that they would touch each other but nothing seems to work. The images are always positioned at the center of their respective containers as shown in the image bellow.</p>
<ol>
<li>On the <strong>left side</strong> I have the left half of the image which I want to position at the very end of its <strong>blue container</strong>.</li>
<li>On the <strong>right side</strong> I have the right half of the image which I want to position at the very start of its <strong>red container</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p><a href="https://i.stack.imgur.com/HJuxk.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.stack.imgur.com/HJuxk.png" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
<p>Here is my JSX code:</p>
<pre><code>return (
      &lt;View
        style={{
          flexDirection: 'row',
        }}
      &gt;
        &lt;Animated.View
          style={{
            width: width / 2,
            height: '100%',
            justifyContent: 'flex-end',
            alignItems: 'flex-end',
            transform: [{ translateX: leftTranslateX }],
            backgroundColor: 'blue',
          }}
        &gt;
          &lt;Image
            source={leftSplash}
            style={{ width: '100%', height: '100%', alignSelf: 'flex-end' }}
            resizeMode=&quot;contain&quot;
          /&gt;
        &lt;/Animated.View&gt;
        &lt;Animated.View
          style={{
            width: width / 2,
            height: '100%',
            justifyContent: 'flex-start',
            alignItems: 'flex-start',
            transform: [{ translateX: rightTranslateX }],
            backgroundColor: 'red',
          }}
        &gt;
          &lt;Image
            source={rightSplash}
            style={{ width: '100%', height: '100%', alignSelf: 'flex-start' }}
            resizeMode=&quot;contain&quot;
          /&gt;
        &lt;/Animated.View&gt;
      &lt;/View&gt;
  );
</code></pre>

answer:
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import { View, Animated, Image } from 'react-native';

const App = () => {
  const width = 375; // Example width for demonstration
  const [leftTranslateX, setLeftTranslateX] = useState(0);
  const [rightTranslateX, setRightTranslateX] = useState(width);

  const slideImages = () => {
    let step = 10; // Adjust this value to control the speed of the animation
    let intervalId = setInterval(() => {
      if (leftTranslateX >= width) {
        clearInterval(intervalId);
        return;
      }
      if (rightTranslateX <= 0) {
        clearInterval(intervalId);
        return;
      }
      setLeftTranslateX(leftTranslateX + step);
      setRightTranslateX(rightTranslateX - step);
    }, 16); // 60 FPS

    return () => clearInterval(intervalId);
  };

  return (
    <View style={{ flex: 1 }}>
      <Animated.View
        style={{
          width: width / 2,
          height: '100%',
          justifyContent: 'center', // Center align the images vertically
          alignItems: 'center', // Center align the images horizontally
          transform: [{ translateX: leftTranslateX }],
          backgroundColor: 'blue',
        }}
      >
        <Image
          source={leftSplash}
          style={{ width: '100%', height: '100%', resizeMode: 'cover' }} // Use cover instead of contain for full-screen scaling
        />
      </Animated.View>
      <Animated.View
        style={{
          width: width / 2,
          height: '100%',
          justifyContent: 'center', // Center align the images vertically
          alignItems: 'center', // Center align the images horizontally
          transform: [{ translateX: rightTranslateX }],
          backgroundColor: 'red',
        }}
      >
        <Image
          source={rightSplash}
          style={{ width: '100%', height: '100%', resizeMode: 'cover' }} // Use cover instead of contain for full-screen scaling
        />
      </Animated.View>
    </View>
  );
};

export default App;

