Title: Fast way to fill array with Objects.
Body: <p>I have to fill an array with a lot of objects. My current Implementation is this:</p>
<pre><code>let useVertices = [];
const len = this.indices.length;
for(let i = 0; i &lt; len; i++){
    let index = this.indices[i]*3;
    useVertices.push(new THREE.Vector3(
        this.vertices[index],
        this.vertices[index+1], 
        this.vertices[index+2])
    );
}
</code></pre>
<p><code>this.indices</code> is an Int32Array with a length of almost 4 million.
<code>this.vertices</code>is a Float32Array with a length of about 650,000.</p>
<p>The implementation shown above takes between 500 and 800 ms.</p>
<p>The Browser I am using is CefSharp, because the website is run in a C# application.</p>
<p>Is it possible to increase the speed of this code?</p>

answer:
import lua

# Assuming 'userdata_obj' is your userdata object
userdata_obj = lua.load_string('return {value1, value2, value3}')

def custom_pairs(userdata):
    # Initialize the state with the userdata
    state = userdata

    def next_state():
        # Check if there are any remaining elements
        if hasattr(state, '__iter__') and not hasattr(state, '_state'):
            state._state = True
            return state
        else:
            return None

    def current_state():
        return getattr(state, '_state', False)

    def finalize():
        # Clean up the resources associated with the userdata
        pass

    while True:
        result = next_state()
        if result is None:
            break
        yield result

        if current_state() and finalize:
            finalize()

# Iterate over the userdata object using the custom iterator
for item in custom_pairs(userdata_obj):
    print(item)

