Title: Why can&#39;t private class fields be deleted?.
Body: <p>It seems it's not possible to delete <code>#</code>private class fields. The syntax doesn't allow it.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>class Example {
    #privatefield = 'some_value';

    deleteField() {
        delete this.#privatefield;
    }
}
</code></pre>
<pre><code>Uncaught SyntaxError: Private fields can not be deleted
</code></pre>
<p>Does anyone know why? What is the rationale behind allowing deletion of normal properties but not of private class fields?</p>

answer:
class Example:
    def __init__(self):
        self._privatefield = 'some_value'

    @property
    def private_field(self):
        return self._privatefield

    @private_field.setter
    def private_field(self, value):
        raise AttributeError("Cannot modify private field directly")

    def delete_private_field(self):
        raise AttributeError("Cannot delete private field")

